    marketTitle: 'The board.',
    marketBody:
      'Live prices from Polymarket and Kalshi. External markets, carried as context — none of them feed the leverage gap. Thin books are labelled, and one contract below resolves on a narrower question than its title suggests.',
    ladderTitle: 'The tariff-rate ladder',
    ladderSub: 'Kalshi · general tariff rate on Canada, January 1, 2027',
    ladderNote: 'A thin book — a few hundred contracts of open interest. Read it as a shape, not a price.',
    pollsEyebrow: 'What the publics say',
    pollsTitle: 'Two countries, one file.',
    pollsBody:
      'Canadians want less concession than their government is offering. Americans want less tariff than their president is imposing. Both facts are measured, and both are inconvenient for the same policy.',
    pollsCanada: 'Canada',
    pollsUs: 'United States',
    timelineEyebrow: 'How we got here',
    timelineTitle: 'From joint review to 50%.',
    quotesEyebrow: 'The two accounts',
    quotesTitle: 'Same night, two stories.',
    takesEyebrow: 'Our read',
    takesTitle: 'Four things this page is saying.',
    watchTitle: 'What we are watching',
    methodEyebrow: 'How the gap works',
    methodTitle: 'One number from two instruments.',
    methodBody:
      'The gap is Canada Goose Index minus Trump strength (100 − Lame-Duck Index). It is derived purely from our two proprietary instruments — transparent and defensible. Everything else on this page is context, deliberately NOT folded into the number.',
    sidesEyebrow: 'The two birds',
    sidesTitle: 'Each side, its own instrument.',
    canadaSub: 'Canada Goose Index',
    usSub: 'Lame-Duck Index',
    strengthLabel: 'residual strength',
    openIndex: 'Open index',
    contextEyebrow: 'Bilateral context',
    contextTitle: 'Signals around the table.',
